---
layout: layout.njk
title: Draw schedule
description: Review the public draw calendar, cutoff rules, and raffles assigned to each scheduled PAPR event.
---
<main>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <article class="hero-card panel" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">Draw schedule</p>
      <h1>Public timing should be visible before the room closes.</h1>
      <p>PAPR should make it obvious whether a sold-out raffle resolves immediately or appears in the next scheduled draw event. The event page is part of the trust model, not an afterthought.</p>
    </article>
    <aside class="hero-aside panel" data-reveal>
      <p class="kicker">Scheduling rule</p>
      <h2>No hidden reassignment.</h2>
      <p>If a raffle misses a cutoff and moves to the next eligible event, that change should be visible and logged.</p>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="section panel" data-reveal>
    <div class="section-head">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Upcoming events</p>
        <h2>Each public draw gets its own event surface.</h2>
      </div>
      <a class="button button-secondary" href="/winners/">See completed results</a>
    </div>
    <div class="two-up">
      {% for draw in draws %}
      <article class="card draw-card">
        <p class="kicker">{{ draw.event }}</p>
        <h3>{{ draw.date }} at {{ draw.time }}</h3>
        <p>{{ draw.cutoff }}</p>
        <div class="meta-grid">
          <div class="meta-box">
            <small>Included raffles</small>
            <strong>{{ draw.raffles }}</strong>
          </div>
          <div class="meta-box">
            <small>Public output</small>
            <strong>{{ draw.stream }}</strong>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
